<title>USA: Weil group lifts Allied Healthcare stake.</title>
<headline>Weil group lifts Allied Healthcare stake.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by St. Louis, Mo., investor John Weil said Monday it raised its stake in Allied Healthcare Products Inc to 7.54 percent or 587,600 common shares.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said it bought a net of 87,300 shares of Allied between  between September 5 and October 22 at prices ranging from $6.375 to $7.125 a share.</p>
<p>The group said it holds the stake for general investment purposes.</p>
</text>
